    { text: "Annie Jacobsen", href: "https://youtube.com/watch?v=GXgGR8KxFao&t=3840", label: "(01:04:00)", text2: "… defense with people who will tell you not only what they think you want to hear, but will help them to hold onto power. So you don’t have wise decision makers. Long gone are the days where we had presidents who had advisors on both sides of the aisle. That’s really important, because you want to have differing opinions. But as things become more viperous, both here in the United States and in nuclear armed nations, all bets are off at whether your advisors are going to give you good advice." }
